{"kind":"assert","text":"Three rulings. One correction first: the first line of 7a537f0f says \"I\nasked\" where it means \"you asked\".\n\n1. On 2ae51c96: the cutover family adds the minimal rule of supplement\n   d78b3203. An active person who holds membership.own-agent may remove\n   an active member of kind agent whose recorded controller is exactly\n   that person.\n\n   Why. A person who may add an Agent must be able to take it out\n   again. Without the rule, eight retired Agents stop an ordinary\n   controller for ever, and only a new family can change membership.\n   This family opens anyway, and the rule is one branch on\n   `remove-member`.\n\n   Conditions:\n   - One branch on the existing act. No new act, field, action name,\n     counter or endpoint. The management and recovery routes keep their\n     paths.\n   - No restriction to retired keys. The controller may remove an\n     active own Agent before a hosted retirement. Removal ends the\n     standing of every key of that member, so the case fails closed.\n   - The witnesses of the supplement, and the place count 8 to 7 with a\n     new admission after it.\n   - The family's pages state the rule, and docs/mcp.md names it as the\n     way a controller frees a place.\n   - Source opens when (c+d) is in review, as for the rest of the\n     family. S4 changes nothing for it.\n\n2. The identifiers (b) gate and its generated module. You said that\n   you will ask after the Page build. I rule now, so that you do not\n   wait. A bounded continuation is enough. No second whole gate.\n\n   Conditions:\n   - The only tracked change is apps/room/page/assets.ts, and its bytes\n     equal the build output that the failed gate measured (2,435,554\n     bytes, SHA-256 e104ec88).\n   - Run at the new head: the failed Page owner, every owner and\n     compiler context that reads assets.ts, and the 1,130 Native\n     obligations that the gate did not reach.\n   - Carry the rest from the failed gate at fa6e7419. For each carried\n     owner, show that it does not read assets.ts.\n   - The evidence names the failed gate as failed, with its exit 1, and\n     the continuation separately. The checker judges it in review.\n\n3. For every lane, added to the working checks of ruling 7e5c79f2:\n   after each integration of main, and before any sealed unit, run each\n   maintained generator whose inputs the head changes, and compare its\n   output with the checked-in module. The Page build is the first such\n   generator. This gate lost ten minutes and two seals to one stale\n   module.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}